+# Place names: sources, uncertainty and curation
+
+The OpenPELAOS layer extends Narrify, the team project by Charalampos Nadiotis
+(n0711), Hussain Jamil and Nikitas Savva. It is a read-only, version-controlled
+pilot in the existing React/Leaflet map. It does not change story submission,
+moderation, accounts, SQLite data, or the project's license status.
+
+## Using it
+
+1. Open the Map tab and choose **Place names**.
+2. Search by a current name, historical form, or words in a sourced explanation.
+   Greek accents, final sigma, and Turkish dotted-I variations are normalized for
+   search only; the original spelling remains on screen.
+3. Use **Origins** to filter by the status of *etymology* claims. A record with
+   historical names but no derivation is **Origin not yet added**.
+4. Open a purple **Aa** marker. Every name variant and explanation links to its
+   source. **Sources and map location** lists publishers, access dates and
+   coordinate evidence.
+5. Nearby stories are the nearest three approved records within 2 km, from the
+   currently selected story category. This is geographic browsing, not an
+   inferred historical link. Loading, API failure and no-result states are distinct.
+6. Return to **Stories** for the original category map.
+
+This is a small pilot, not a language-origin classification of the island.
+Settlement points are approximate reference locations, not historical boundaries.
+The layer is bundled with the frontend and needs no additional network requests;
+the existing story API and map tiles still require their usual connections.
+
+## Evidence and initial records
+
+Sources were consulted on 20 October 2026. Summaries are short paraphrases;
+source photographs, maps and full text are not bundled.
+
+- **Lefkosia / Nicosia:** [Nicosia Municipality](https://www.nicosia.org.cy/en-GB/discover/nicosia/nicosia/names/)
+  records earlier city names including Ledra, Lefkothea and Lefkousia. The pilot
+  does not choose an etymology for the present names.
+- **Anogyra:** [Cyprus Deputy Ministry of Tourism](https://www.visitcyprus.com/discover-cyprus/rural/villages-rural/anogyra-village-2/)
+  gives two possible explanations: the anagyris plant, and ano plus Gyroi.
+  Both stay visible as possible explanations.
+- **Lazanias:** [Cyprus Deputy Ministry of Tourism](https://www.visitcyprus.com/discover-cyprus/culture/sites-and-monuments/saint-george-s-church-lazanias-village/)
+  links the name to Lusignan. It is labelled source-reported, not an independent
+  scholarly resolution.
+
+Coordinates and selected modern variants are credited to **GeoNames**, under its
+[CC BY terms](https://www.geonames.org/export/). Permanent records:
+[Nicosia 146268](https://www.geonames.org/146268/nicosia.html),
+[Anogyra 146810](https://www.geonames.org/146810/anogyra.html),
+[Lazanias 146393](https://www.geonames.org/146393/lazanias.html).
+Lazanias coordinates and variants were also checked in the
+[GeoNames populated-place listing](https://www.geonames.org/advanced-search.html?country=CY&featureClass=P&q=&startRow=450).
+Map tiles keep their existing OpenStreetMap attribution.
+
+The user-supplied settlement-name infographic is visual inspiration only.
+Its compiler credit remains separate from the Narrify team credits.
+Its raster, boundaries and settlement classifications were not imported.
+
+## Adding a record
+
+Edit `frontend/src/data/placeNames.json` in a reviewable branch. Each place has:
+
+- A stable unique `id`, `displayName`, numeric latitude/longitude, and a
+  `locationSourceId` referencing a source in that record.
+- `editorialStatus`: `draft` or `published`. Only valid published records render.
+- `aliases`: original `name`, optional language tag, `kind` (current, historical,
+  variant), and `sourceId`. Language of a name is not an ethnic or territorial claim.
+- `claims`: stable unique ID, `kind` (name-history or etymology), `summary`,
+  `status`, and one or more valid `sourceIds`.
+- `sources`: ID, title, publisher, absolute HTTPS URL and ISO access date.
+  Coordinate listing evidence can be supplied in `coordinateEvidenceUrl`.
+
+Use **reported** for an explanation explicitly made by the source, **proposed**
+when the source presents it as possible, and **disputed** when sources document
+disagreement. These labels describe the evidence, not a truth score. For no
+sourced origin explanation, omit etymology claims; the UI supplies an unresolved
+state. Do not invent origins, fill gaps using AI text, or treat a modern name
+variant as proof of derivation. Keep distinct explanations as separate claims.
+
+Invalid records, missing source references, duplicate place IDs and drafts are
+excluded at runtime. Tests also reject invalid committed pilot data so an editor
+cannot silently lose a record. A pull request is the review step for publishing
+new records; there is no public editing API in this pilot.
+
+## Validation
+
+The Jest configuration maps the installed React Router CommonJS entry points
+for the older CRA test resolver; dependency versions remain unchanged.
+
+From `frontend`:
+
+```sh
+npm ci
+CI=true npm test -- --watchAll=false --runInBand
+npm run build
+```
+
+The focused tests cover source integrity, draft exclusion, multilingual search,
+origin status filtering, competing explanations, approved-only nearby results,
+the card's source links, and switching map layers. Existing backend demo checks
+remain documented in the main README. No research impact or deployment is
+claimed by adding this feature.
